{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_e3qskppgdn2hlm6txkhefcf22cnezhfzqbafssx6rzec5ail7pwq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 4 tests pass. The implementation correctly translates the C minidb (mdb) project to safe, idiomatic Rust:\n\n**Summary:**\n- **`Mdb::create`** — writes the superblock (text format), initializes index file with zeroed freeptr + hash bucket pointers, and creates an empty data file.\n- **`Mdb::open`** — parses the text superblock and opens index/data files for read/write.\n- **`Mdb::read/write/delete`** — chain through the bucket linked list, comparing keys (with null-padded key comparison via `bytes_to_str`).\n- **`hash`** — replicated the C hash exactly: `sum(byte * index)` with wrapping arithmetic.\n- **`data_alloc`** — walks the data file looking for a contiguous run of zero bytes ≥ `size + 2`, matching the C implementation's quirky behavior of using non-zero markers to delimit allocations (start_ptr = first zero, end_ptr = position after next non-zero byte).\n- **`index_alloc/index_free`** — maintains a free list rooted at offset 0 of the index file.\n- All file I/O uses little-endian binary representation (matching x86 native byte order in C `fwrite`).\n- No `unsafe`, no FFI — pure safe Rust using `std::fs::File` and `std::io`.\n\nThe tests `happy_test0`, `reopen_test1`, `load_test2`, and `load_test3` all pass."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1004,"cache_read_input_tokens":52467,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1004,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"56872e84-e92c-4110-a931-11f61121293e","uuid":"46bbf7d6-ba22-468e-aee0-b59f4d039fe3"}
